    <statement><p>Classify each of the sentences below as an atomic statement, a molecular statement, or not a statement at all. If the statement is molecular, say what kind it is (conjuction, disjunction, conditional, biconditional, negation).</p>
<p><ol>
<li>
<p>Everybody can be fooled sometimes.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Every natural number greater than 1 is either prime or composite.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Go to your room!</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The Broncos will win the Super Bowl, or I'll eat my hat.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>This shirt is not black.</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
